Declare source as integer with value 7. Declare p as pointer to integer with value Address of source. Declare cp as pointer to constant integer with value p. Say Value at cp. Declare rp as restricted pointer to integer with value Address of source. Set value at rp to 8. Say source. Declare v as volatile integer with value 3. Set v to 4. Say v. Declare atom as atomic integer with value 5. Declare ap as pointer to atomic integer with value Address of atom. Set value at ap to 6. Say atom. Declare zero as constant integer. Say zero. Procedure local returns integer: Declare x as constant integer with value 9. Say x. Return x. End procedure. Say Call local done. Procedure ptr returns integer: Declare y as integer with value 2. Declare q as constant pointer to integer with value Address of y. Set value at q to 3. Return y. End procedure. Say Call ptr done.
